# Sitemap moods are static files (public/<mood>.html). Pages serves those at
# /<mood> on its own, and redirects /<mood>.html to /<mood> (308), same as
# /p.html → /p. Do not add `/<mood> /<mood>.html 200` or `/<mood> /p 200`:
# the .html proxy loops with that 308, and a /p proxy hides the mood head.
# Trailing slashes match the sitemap (no slash).
# /blaaah stays the share page and stays out of the sitemap.
/classic/ /classic 301
/confused/ /confused 301
/shocked/ /shocked 301
/annoyed/ /annoyed 301
/disgusted/ /disgusted 301
/suspicious/ /suspicious 301
/amused/ /amused 301
/scared/ /scared 301
/bored/ /bored 301
/offended/ /offended 301
/curious/ /curious 301
/blaaah/ /blaaah 301
/blaaah /p 200
